  1	//! `k6_observe`: one K6 kernel observation per process (T3 D1 §4.8; K6 plan
  2	//! §2). Observation only: it prints JSONL on stdout and asserts no time or
  3	//! memory bound. See `H/README.md` ("K6") for the schema.
  4	//!
  5	//! Exit codes: 0 completed (an M03 refusal is an outcome, not an error);
  6	//! 2 usage; 3 refused by the binary; 4 internal error. A heap-cap refusal
  7	//! aborts (SIGABRT) after the allocator's marker.
  8	
